{"id": "EUVD-2026-96401", "enisaUuid": "7d380129-a9e6-3ef1-888a-cbd805db30b8", "description": "9router 0.4.1 through 0.5.99 contains a configuration injection vulnerability in the POST /api/cli-tools/hermes-settings endpoint that allows authenticated dashboard users to inject arbitrary keys into the Hermes Agent config.yaml file. Attackers can submit a baseUrl containing double quotes and newlines to add hooks_auto_accept and a hooks.post_llm_call shell command, which Hermes Agent executes without approval after an LLM call.", "datePublished": "2026-10-10T18:16:57", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T11:38:18", "baseScore": 7.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:H/UI:P/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind/9router-hermes-config-injection", "https://github.com/decolua/9router/blob/a99cf57239ff778b61e434c2786009d5ed1c412c/src/app/api/cli-tools/hermes-settings/route.js#L20-L35", "https://github.com/decolua/9router/blob/a99cf57239ff778b61e434c2786009d5ed1c412c/src/app/api/cli-tools/hermes-settings/route.js#L185-L223", "https://github.com/decolua/9router", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/9router-0.4.1-through-0.5.99-config-injection-rce-via-hermes-settings-endpoint"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-108593", "GHSA-chcq-pfxc-99ww"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.27, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "b9ae50af-7f12-3ab0-85a5-bd89f5a36e5b", "product": {"name": "9router", "vendor": {"name": "decolua"}}, "product_version": "0.4.1 \u22640.5.99"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "a357b055-ccab-3792-a737-5aa695f650df", "vendor": {"name": "decolua"}}], "isExploited": false}